ary\": \"Gastrointestinal and hepatic conditions impose important drug-use restrictions\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Certain pre-existing conditions significantly limit therapeutic options. Aspirin is contraindicated in patients with gastric or duodenal ulcers due to its irritant and antiplatelet effects [Data: Relationships (7486)]. Warfarin is contraindicated in chronic liver disease because of altered metabolism via CYP2C9 and CYP1A2 inhibition, which can potentiate anticoagulation [Data: Relationships (5766)]. Additionally, alprostadil (implied via amoxicillin-clavulanate) is linked to obstructive jaundice as a rare but serious adverse effect [Data: Relationships (17092)]. These contraindications stress the necessity of thorough patient history assessment before initiating therapy.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 6.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community includes widely used medications with significant contraindications and adverse effects in vulnerable populations, warranting moderate-to-high clinical vigilance.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782128774, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1404, "prompt_tokens": 7083, "total_tokens": 8487, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"Bisphosphonates, Calcium-Vitamin D Supplements, and Associated Adverse Effects\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on bisphosphonate drugs (e.g., zoledronic acid, ibandronate, risedronate) and calcium-vitamin D combination supplements (e.g., calcium carbonate D3 tablets, children's vitamin D calcium), along with related diseases, side